&gt;&gt;&gt; Optimal	Bedrooms, Engineering
&gt;&gt; Suitable	Blades, Hospitals
X Inadvisable 	Workshops

Tools Recommended: Cooking, Tree-cutting
Notes: Used in special components

Half Nickel, half titanium. It's an important alloy used for high tech actuators and robotics due to its superelasticity and shape memory features, and it's used for surgical tools and implants as well. These qualities also allow it to perform fairly well against heat and ballistic impacts, but not so much blunt force, and tools made of nitinol are tough and effective. The combination of strength and ductility give it superior resiliancy to damage. It's also difficult to work with.</description>
